---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import CopyButton from '../components/CopyButton.astro';
import FooterNav from '../components/FooterNav.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import { highlightCode } from '../lib/highlight';

const movieTemplate = `---
year: {{ year }}
director: {{ directors | wikilink }}
genre: {{ genres }}
---

# {{ title }}

{{ plot | blockquote }}

## Cast

{{ cast | slice:0,4 | table }}`;

const markdownOutput = `---
year: 1999
director: ["[[Lana Wachowski]]","[[Lilly Wachowski]]"]
genre: ["Action","Sci-fi"]
---

# The Matrix

> A hacker discovers that reality is a simulation and joins a rebellion against its machines.

## Cast

| Actor | Role |
| - | - |
| Keanu Reeves | Neo |
| Laurence Fishburne | Morpheus |
| Carrie-Anne Moss | Trinity |
| Hugo Weaving | Agent Smith |`;
---

<BaseLayout markdownPath="/index.md">
  <main>
    <section class="hero-shell">
      <SiteHeader />
      <div class="hero-grid">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <h1>The templating language for Markdown.</h1>
          <p class="lede">Knap lets you create reusable templates that turn data into structured Markdown documents.</p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="button button-primary" href="/logic">Read the language guide</a>
            <a class="button button-secondary" href="/api">Add Knap to a project</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="code-window doc-code-numbered" aria-label="Knap template example">
          <div class="code-window-bar"><span>template.md</span><span class="code-window-actions"><CopyButton /></span></div>
          <pre><code class="language-knap" data-language="knap" set:html={highlightCode(movieTemplate, 'knap', true)} /></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="install-strip" aria-label="Installation">
      <div><span class="install-label">Install</span><code>pnpm add knap</code></div>
      <a href="/api#quick-start">Quick start →</a>
    </section>

    <section class="markdown-native" aria-labelledby="markdown-native-title">
      <header class="markdown-native-heading">
        <h2 id="markdown-native-title">Parse&nbsp;it. Knap&nbsp;it. Quick, format it.</h2>
        <div>
          <p>Knap is a simple language designed to generate Markdown in a repeatably. Knap filters help manipulate app data to generate <a href="/filters/table">tables</a>, <a href="/filters/link">links</a>, <a href="/filters/list">lists</a>, <a href="/filters/footnote">footnotes</a>, <a href="/filters/blockquote">blockquotes</a>, and <a href="/filters">more</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </header>
      <div class="markdown-transform">
        <CodeBlock label="template.md" code={movieTemplate} showLineNumbers />
        <CodeBlock language="md" label="note.md" code={markdownOutput} showLineNumbers />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="feature-grid" aria-labelledby="why-knap">
      <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="why-knap">Made for applications that create Markdown.</h2></div>
      <div class="feature-cards">
        <article><span class="feature-index">01</span><h3>Safe by design</h3><p>An AST interpreter handles templates. Knap does not use eval or execute arbitrary JavaScript.</p></article>
        <article><span class="feature-index">02</span><h3>Application-owned</h3><p>Apps supply variables, asynchronous resolvers, and custom filters. Knap is independent of any host environment.</p></article>
        <article><span class="feature-index">03</span><h3>Useful diagnostics</h3><p>Errors and warnings include stable codes, messages, lines, and columns for editor tooling and helpful user feedback.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="used-by" aria-labelledby="used-by-knap">
      <header class="used-by-heading"><div><h2 id="used-by-knap">Powered by Knap.</h2></div><p>Knap is the shared template language behind tools that turn web pages and imported data into durable Markdown.</p></header>
      <div class="used-by-list">
        <a href="https://obsidian.md/clipper" class="used-by-card"><div class="used-by-copy"><h3>Obsidian Web Clipper</h3><span>Renders page data, highlights, selectors, and custom variables through user-defined templates before saving them as Markdown.</span></div><strong aria-hidden="true">↗</strong></a>
        <a href="https://community.obsidian.md/plugins/obsidian-importer" class="used-by-card"><div class="used-by-copy"><h3>Obsidian Importer</h3><span>Applies templates and filters to imported fields so notes from other apps arrive in a consistent Markdown structure.</span></div><strong aria-hidden="true">↗</strong></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="path-grid" aria-label="Documentation paths">
      <a href="/variables"><span>Start with</span><strong>Variables</strong><small>{'{{ title }}'} →</small></a>
      <a href="/logic"><span>Then add</span><strong>Logic</strong><small>{'{% if author %}'} →</small></a>
      <a href="/filters"><span>Shape with</span><strong>Filters</strong><small>{'| trim | title'} →</small></a>
    </section>

    <footer class="site-footer"><a class="wordmark footer-mark" href="/">Knap</a><FooterNav /><p>Open source under the MIT license.</p><a href="https://github.com/obsidianmd/knap">GitHub ↗</a></footer>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
